PATCH 159: the model-loader filename-suffix builder cluster (FUN_1000_2733/2762/2765/276e/27e2/27f7/280a,
asm 0x12733..0x1280a) -- the exact sibling of FUN_1000_26fc (patch 099), reached on the ACCEPT mission
cascade (BATTLES->OK->ACCEPT) via 4308->18dc->183f->19d1->2733.  NOT reached by any of the 19 verify flows
(a bare host-ptr deref of the cs-data tables would already SIGSEGV them) -> behaviour-neutral for verify.

  These seg-0f69 functions read a per-extension method vtable held in CS-relative data
  (cs:0x2b6a current-slot + 4-slot handle table, cs:0x2b74 type table, cs:0x2b7e ext-byte + variant
  suffixes, cs:0x2b88 attr/load / 0x2b8e open / 0x2b94 close / 0x2b9a read / 0x2ba6 seek handler-vector
  columns).  The correct CS-data base is g_mem+0xf690 (the seg-0f69 module is loaded there: 2733's code
  at image 0x12733 = 0xf690+0x30a3), NOT the 0x12b.. host offset Ghidra kept after decoding under
  CS=0x1000.  The driver-built filename buffer is a DGROUP near offset (param_2) -> g_mem+0x1c000+off.
  Widths: DAT_1000_2b7e is a BYTE (asm `mov cs:0x2b7e,al`); the slot/type/vtable entries are WORDs.
  The OPEN handler's carry (276e) is threaded via g_fist_cf (Ghidra folded it to a stale pre-call test).

  2733  = attr-probe + full LOAD: for each ext variant, INT 21h AH=4300; first hit dispatches
          cs:[variant*2+0x2b88] (variant0 = 0f69:0x318e = `mov es,ax; call 2593` = the batch reader).
  2762/2765 = mid-instruction re-entries into 2733's dispatch tail (di doubled / already-doubled).
  276e  = streaming OPEN: allocate a slot, INT 21h AH=4300 probe, dispatch cs:[variant*2+0x2b8e]
          (0f69:0x3195 open+lseek-size), store {handle,type} into the slot.
  27e2/27f7/280a = per-slot CLOSE(0x2b94)/READ(0x2b9a)/SEEK(0x2ba6): look up the slot's type, call the
          handler with bx=handle (handlers 0f69:0x31d7/0x31e1/0x31eb = INT 21h AH=3e/3f/42).

  NB the handler-vtable targets (0f69:0x318e/0x3195/0x31d7/0x31e1/0x31eb..) are NOT yet promoted FUNs, so
  fist_icall_near traps them safely (return 0) -- crash-free but inert: the actual model open/read is
  unblocked once those primitives are promoted (SeedServiceVecs seed + re-decompile), the next frontier.

  ALSO fixes the byte-identical sibling FUN_1000_2688 (asm 0x12688, same cs:0x2b6a/0x2b8e tables) with
  the identical reconstruction -- a second streaming-OPEN entry that carried the same wild-deref.

